comments.body:
@wjykyhhh Thanks for checking the saved account's own isolated credentials. Your snapshot is outside the scope of my earlier patch: it can correct Pro to Max when the credential already contains a Max rate-limit tier, but it cannot derive Max from both subscriptionType=pro and rateLimitTier=default_claude_ai. My earlier explanation was too broad for that case.

I also checked main at b1e8eb15a668bbccfcd46977c75602ceaa4d66b3: takeClaudeDir still returns early when the access and refresh tokens are unchanged, before comparing subscription metadata. That is a separate synchronization gap when the CLI actually updates its metadata without changing tokens; it does not explain your captured case, since that isolated CLI metadata was still Pro too.

I have not verified a supported noninteractive command that refreshes the upstream subscription metadata independently of token renewal, or a release that fixes your exact snapshot. A successful quota refresh alone is not proof that subscription metadata was refreshed, and the presence of a model-specific usage window is not enough to infer the billing plan. I would not recommend changing the saved plan or tier by hand from those signals. The existing fork patch should be treated as the Max-tier mapping fix only, not a confirmed fix for this follow-up report.

